                "entry_id": "a3159a7a-2b49-38a7-8568-06bcc4d6c4dc",
                "word": "moxa",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f2886259-74bf-4917-9344-50f75fc8c013",
                        "entry_id": "a3159a7a-2b49-38a7-8568-06bcc4d6c4dc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "moxas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4786a9bc-c7a0-3589-9f6e-48519f5817eb",
                        "entry_id": "a3159a7a-2b49-38a7-8568-06bcc4d6c4dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A woolly material obtained from the dried leaves of an Asian species of mugwort, such as Artemisia argyi, as used in moxibustion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea37b481-cb1c-4735-ab0c-8a84aed8fb5d",
                                "sense_id": "4786a9bc-c7a0-3589-9f6e-48519f5817eb",
                                "text": "And thereupon she burned with her Moxa (of which hereafter) on my feet and knees, (to my best remembrance) about twenty little Escars, which looked like lit∣tle gray specks, without raising any blisters, or causing any after-pain; whereupon also all the pain of the Gout vanish’d."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e37533d4-e8ea-49a0-b839-250761e08b94",
                                "sense_id": "4786a9bc-c7a0-3589-9f6e-48519f5817eb",
                                "text": "Moxa is celebrated in the eastern countries, for preventing and curing many disorders, by being burnt on the skin: a little cone of moxa, laid on the part previously moistened, and set on fire at top, burns down with a temperate glowing heat, and produces a dark coloured spot, the exulceration of which is promoted by applying a little garlic, and the ulcer either healed up when the eschar separates, or kept running for a length of time, as different circumstances may require."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb084090-e4d1-379d-bbef-bc6e027e919c",
                        "entry_id": "a3159a7a-2b49-38a7-8568-06bcc4d6c4dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any other substance used in moxibustion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1de5dcc6-3540-4b39-8652-9427e542e170",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3159a7a-2b49-38a7-8568-06bcc4d6c4dc",
                        "source_sense_description": "woolly material obtained from mugwort leaves",
                        "target_lang_word": "moxa",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moxa",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6e701a4-da8b-3b2e-8124-0d1c98a34589",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4c59d5-d785-3727-b551-36e5ab0a1dd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Substance telle que la poudre de feuille séchée d’armoise, le coton ou l’étoupe, souvent à la forme d’un petit cône, que l’on applique sur quelque partie du corps et à laquelle on met le feu. Utilisé dans la médecine asiatique traditionnelle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "984eafe4-5c58-36e0-b066-9d647b622943",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4c59d5-d785-3727-b551-36e5ab0a1dd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cautérisation lente utilisant du moxa."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3b6980f-ab20-42d6-a4b5-4f3c0a268d1e",
                                                "sense_id": "984eafe4-5c58-36e0-b066-9d647b622943",
                                                "text": "Appliquer le moxa."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "316b1607-b369-4754-bbdd-c90e18274ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "984eafe4-5c58-36e0-b066-9d647b622943",
                                                "text": "On lui a appliqué deux ou trois moxas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3823e99e-2cfa-3168-8999-617754744247",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4c59d5-d785-3727-b551-36e5ab0a1dd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Remède, calmant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "679c7c3b-c040-49f6-8078-2a3f6f5ef0aa",
                                                "sense_id": "3823e99e-2cfa-3168-8999-617754744247",
                                                "text": "Il souffre tant à la tête qu’il ne sentait pas les moxas qu’on lui appliquait jadis pour essayer de le distraire ; mais monsieur Brousson, qu’il a pris pour médecin les a défendus, en prétendant que c’était une affection nerveuse, une inflammation de nerfs, pour laquelle il fallait des sangsues au cou et de l’opium sur la tête."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c5e2d90-e372-4223-bc06-0c39f4e5c292",
                                                "sense_id": "3823e99e-2cfa-3168-8999-617754744247",
                                                "text": "En effet, aucun ennui, aucun spleen ne résiste au moxa qu'on se pose à l'âme en se donnant une manie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa59b0fd-40f6-4982-b651-9dea928f253b",
                                                "sense_id": "3823e99e-2cfa-3168-8999-617754744247",
                                                "text": "Aussi, lorsque les battements de ce coeur s'arrêtent faute d'ouvrage, la ville n'est plusqu'un corps paralysé auquel on ne peut rendre le mouvement que par le moxa des commandes ministérielles et le galvanisme des fournitures roales;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
